  "readmeFile": "ReadmeNuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Headless CLI deploy: a deploy target (DeployInfo in designer.settings.Development.json) now has an AllowCliDeploy flag (default false). The deploy sub-command sends to the current deploy target only when this flag is true, regardless of the deploy method (FileSystem or FTPS); a target without it is refused with a message that names the setting. This replaces the previous rule that allowed every FileSystem target and refused every FTPS target - a local folder is no guarantee of a development server, so the user's explicit setting is the boundary, the same way AllowCliSqlAccess gates the sql sub-command. The \"Add deploy target\" dialog has a matching \"Allow deploy from CLI\" checkbox, and template-create --deploy-dir marks the target it creates as allowed.\nEmbedded spec docs (ProjectSettings.md) document the new property.\nRequires Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.31.",
